er\nwhat do i look when inspect the packaging.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\ntraining text example:\n<|im_start|>system\nYou are an agricultural assistant. Answer the farmer's question clearly, correctly, and concisely, in plain English.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nwhat do i look when inspect the packaging.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nLook for signs of tampering, such as broken seals or mismatched packaging, which may indicate that the product is fake.<|im_end|>\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"489def13","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Are the saved adapters really trained?\nLoRA starts with every **B matrix = 0**. A trained adapter has clearly non-zero B. This reads the weights straight from\nthe `.safetensors` files - no model needed - and also checks that LoRA and QLoRA are *different* weights.","metadata":{}},{"id":"77ba3597","cell_type":"code","source":"for name, path in ADAPTERS.items():\n    info = inspect_adapter(path)\n    print(name, {k: (round(v, 6) if isinstance(v, float) else v) for k, v in info.items()})\n    print(\"   ->\", \"TRAINED (B matrices are non-zero)\" if info[\"lora_B_mean_abs\"] > 1e-5 else \"!!! looks UNTRAINED (B ~ 0)\")\nif len(ADAPTERS) > 1:\n    names = list(ADAPTERS)\n    print(f\"\\n{names[0]} vs {names[1]}:\", compare_adapters(ADAPTERS[names[0]], ADAPTERS[names[1]]))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T19:25:39.035086Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T19:25:39.035648Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T19:25:39.111975Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-12T19:25:39.03562Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T19:25:39.11114Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"lora {'tensors': 224, 'lora_B_tensors': 112, 'lora_B_mean_abs': 0.004656, 'lora_B_all_zero_tensors': 0, 'lora_A_mean_abs': 0.01436}\n   -> TRAINED (B matrices are non-zero)\nqlora {'tensors': 224, 'lora_B_tensors': 112, 'lora_B_mea