n\nQ: which type of family do green manure crops belongs to. \n  REF : leguminous \n  PRED: Family Leguminosae\n\nQ: which cassava variety was developed by the International Institute of Tropical Agriculture (IITA) and is popular in many African countries. \n  REF : TME 419 \n  PRED: Kintan 1\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":27},{"id":"858a8657","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 11. RAG hook demo - how this connects to the Fine-Tuning + RAG project\n`run_arm(llm, \"A\"|\"B\"|\"C\"|\"D\", question, retriever)` implements four of the five ablation arms from your roadmap\n(A base, B base+RAG, C fine-tuned, D fine-tuned+RAG). **The only thing you will replace later is the retriever**\n(TF-IDF here -> FAISS + BGE-M3 hybrid retriever). The retriever contract is just: `retriever(question, k) -> list[str]`.\n\n> This demo's \"knowledge base\" is the training answers, only to prove the plumbing works. The adapters were trained\n> *without* facts in the prompt, so Arm D quality is a research question for the RAG phase, not something to claim here.","metadata":{}},{"id":"d7b9f8a3","cell_type":"code","source":"retriever = TfidfRetriever(list(train_ds[\"answer\"]))      # stand-in; replace with Golden-Fact retriever later\nfor q in [\"Which pest sucks sap from bean plants and distorts leaves?\", \"Can maize grow in clay soil?\"]:\n    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 90 + f\"\\nQ: {q}\")\n    for arm in [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"]:\n        r = run_arm(llm, arm, q, retriever=retriever, ft_adapter=\"qlora\", max_new_tokens=120)\n        print(f\"\\n[{arm}] {r['desc']}\\n   {textwrap.shorten(r['answer'], 300)}\")\n        if r[\"facts\"]:\n            print(\"   facts used:\", [textwrap.shorten(f, 70) for f in r[\"facts\"]])","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T20:15:43.405386Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T20:15:43.406038Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T20:16:00.966461Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-12T20:15:43.406009Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T20:16:00.965781Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"\n==========================================================================================\nQ: Which pest sucks sap from bean plants and distorts leaves?\n\n[A] Base LLM\n   The pest you're describing is likely a bean leafroller (Elaeagnus sp.). This insect feeds on the sap of bean plants and causes significant damage by feeding on the underside of leaves, which can distort their shape and reduce plant health.\n\n[B] Base LLM + RAG\n   I am not sure. The information provided does not mention any specific pests that suck sap from bean plants or distort their leaves.\n   facts used: ['bean cakes, bean bread, and bean porridge.', 'bean cakes, bean bread, and bean porridge.', 'bean cakes, bean bread, and bean porridge.']\n\n[C] Fine-tuned\n   Bean leafhoppers\n\n[D] Fine-tuned + RAG\n   Bean aphids\n   facts used: ['bean cakes, bean bread, and bean porridge.', 'bean cakes, bean bread, and bean porridge.', 'bean cakes, bean bread, and bean porridge.']\n\n==========================================================================================\nQ: Can maize grow in clay soil?\n\n[A] Base LLM\n   Yes, maize can grow in clay soil, but it may require additional management practices to ensure optimal growth. Clay soils often have poor drainage and high water retention capacity, which can lead to root rot if not managed properly. To improve conditions for maize in clay soil: 1. **Soil [...]\n\n[B] Base LLM + RAG\n   Yes, maize can grow in clay soil, but proper management is crucial due to its characteristic of retaining water and draining poorly, leading to potential issues like waterlogging and compaction that can hinder root penetration and nutrient uptake.\n   facts used: ['es, maize can grow in clay soil. However, clay soil has certain [...]', 'es, maize can grow in clay soil. However, clay soil has certain [...]', 'es, maize can grow in clay soil. However, clay soil has certain [...]']\n\n[C] Fine-tuned\n   Maize can tolerate a range of soil types, including clay soils, but it prefers well-drained sandy loam or loamy soils with good fertility and adequate moisture. Clay soils may be more prone to waterlogging if drainage is poor, which could negatively impact maize growth and yield.\n\n[D] Fine-tuned + RAG\n   Maize can grow in clay soil, but it may require additional management practices to overcome some of its limitations. Clay soil is known for retaining moisture and poor drainage, which can lead to waterlogging and root suffocation if not properly managed. Additionally, clay soil can be [...]\n   facts used: ['es, maize can grow in clay soil. However, clay soil has certain [...]', 'es, maize can grow in clay soil. However, clay soil has certain [...]', 'es, maize can grow in clay soil. However, clay soil has certain [...]']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":28},{"id":"d5a531df","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 12. Package everything for deployment and the next project\nCreates `/kaggle/working/agri_deploy/` containing: `agri_llm.py`, the Gradio app, `requirements.txt`, both adapters,\nevaluation CSV/JSON, and a **model card whose numbers are filled from your measured results** (nothing invented).","metadata":{}},{"id":"aa43700a","cell_type":"code","source":"%%writefile /kaggle/working/agri_deploy/app_gradio.py\n\"\"\"\napp_gradio.py - Gradio demo for the agricultural Q&A fine-tunes.\n\nWorks on: Hugging Face Spaces (Gradio SDK), Kaggle/Colab (share=True), your laptop.\n\nConfigure with environment variables (no code edits needed):\n  AGRI_ADAPTERS   JSON  {\"lora\": \"<repo-or-folder>\", \"qlora\": \"<repo-or-folder>\"}\n  AGRI_BASE_MODEL base model id (default Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct)\n  AGRI_4BIT       \"1\" -> load base in 4-bit (needs an NVIDIA GPU + bitsandbytes;\n                  ~1.2 GB of weights, fits a 4 GB laptop GPU)\n  HF_TOKEN        only for private repos\nPlace this file next to agri_llm.py (or keep the repo layout: ../src/agri_llm.py).\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nfor _p in (HERE, os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"src\")):\n    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(_p, \"agri_llm.py\")):\n        sys.path.insert(0, _p)\n        break\n\nimport gradio as gr\nfrom agri_llm import AgriLLM, DEFAULT_BASE_MODEL\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"AGRI_BASE_MODEL\", DEFAULT_BASE_MODEL)\nADAPTERS = json.loads(os.environ.get(\"AGRI_ADAPTERS\", \"{}\"))\nFOUR_BIT = os.environ.get(\"AGRI_4BIT\", \"0\") == \"1\"\nDISCLAIMER = (\"Research prototype - fine-tuned on community Q&A data, **not** a substitute \"\n              \"for professional agricultural advice.\")\nEXAMPLES = [\"How do I control aphids on cotton?\", \"Can maize grow in clay soil?\",\n            \"Which pest feeds on the sap of bean plants and distorts the leaves?\",\n            \"What causes shriveling and rotting of bean seeds?\"]\n\n_llm = None\n\n\ndef get_llm() -> AgriLLM:\n    global _llm\n    if _llm is None:\n        _llm = AgriLLM(BASE, ADAPTERS, load_in_4bit=FOUR_BIT, hf_token=os.environ.get(\"HF_TOKEN\"))\n    return _llm\n\n\ndef parse_facts(text):\n    lines = [l.strip(\" -\\u2022\\t\") for l in (text or \"\").splitlines()]\n    return [l for l in lines if l] or None\n\n\ndef respond(question, mode, facts_text, max_new_tokens):\n    if not question or not question.strip():\n        return \"Please type a question.\"\n    llm = get_llm()\n    facts = parse_facts(facts_text)\n    modes = llm.modes if mode == \"Compare all\" else [mode]\n    parts = []\n    for m in modes:\n        ans = llm.generate(question, mode=m, facts=facts, max_new_tokens=int(max_new_tokens))\n        parts.append(f\"### {m}\\n{ans}\")\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)\n\n\ndef build_ui():\n    choices = [\"Compare all\", \"base\"] + list(ADAPTERS.keys())\n    with gr.Blocks(title=\"Agri Q&A - LoRA / QLoRA demo\") as demo:\n        gr.Markdown(f\"# Agricultural Q&A - fine-tuned Qwen2.5-1.5B\\n{DISCLAIMER}\")\n        q = gr.Textbox(label=\"Farming question\", lines=2)\n        mode = gr.Radio(choices, value=choices[0], label=\"Model\")\n        facts = gr.Textbox(label=\"(Optional) paste verified facts - one per line - to try RAG-style answers\",\n                           lines=3)\n        n = gr.Slider(40, 300, value=160, step=20, label=\"Max answer length (tokens)\")\n        out = gr.Markdown()\n        gr.Button(\"Answer\", variant=\"primary\").click(respond, [q, mode, facts, n], out)\n        gr.Examples(EXAMPLES, inputs=q)\n    return demo\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    build_ui().queue().launch(share=os.environ.get(\"GRADIO_SHARE\", \"0\") == \"1\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T20:19:05.251452Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T20:19:05.252255Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T20:19:05.258599Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-12T20:19:05.252223Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T20:19:05.257805Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Overwriting /kaggle/working/agri_deploy/app_gradio.py\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":29},{"id":"a69d00dc","cell_type":"code","source":"%%writefile /kaggle/working/agri_deploy/requirements.txt\n# Deployment requirements (CPU Space / local). On a GPU box keep the CUDA torch you already have.\n--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu\ntorch\ntransformers>=4.46.0\npeft>=0.13.0\naccelerate>=0.34.0\nhuggingface_hub>=0.24.0\nsafetensors\nsentencepiece\nscikit-learn          # only for the optional TF-IDF demo retriever\ngradio>=4.0           # for app_gradio.py\nstreamlit>=1.35.0     # for app.py\n# bitsandbytes        # add ONLY for 4-bit inference on an NVIDIA GPU (AGRI_4BIT=1)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T20:19:34.400906Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T20:19:34.401793Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T20:19:34.406808Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-12T20:19:34.401761Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T20:19:34.406086Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Overwriting /kaggle/working/agri_deploy/requirements.txt\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":30},{"id":"1d6416ea","cell_type":"code","source":"# copy adapters next to the code\nos.makedirs(f\"{OUT}/adapters\", exist_ok=True)\nfor name, path in ADAPTERS.items():\n    shutil.copytree(path, f\"{OUT}/adapters/{name}\", dirs_exist_ok=True)\n\ndef df_to_md(df):\n    head = \"| model | \" + \" | \".join(df.columns) + \" |\\n|\" + \"---|\" * (len(df.columns) + 1)\n    body = \"\\n\".join(\"| \" + str(i) + \" | \" + \" | \".join(f\"{v:.4f}\" for v in row) + \" |\" for i, row in df.iterrows())\n    return head + \"\\n\" + body\n\nCARD = f'''---\nbase_model: {BASE_MODEL_ID}\nlibrary_name: peft\ntags: [lora, qlora, agriculture, question-answering]\nlicense: apache-2.0\n---\n# Agricultural Q&A adapters (LoRA / QLoRA) for {BASE_MODEL_ID}\n\nAdapters fine-tuned on a 4,000-example subsample of `KisanVaani/agriculture-qa-english-only`\n(500 validation / 500 test, seed 42). They are **adapters**, not full models: load them on top of the base model.\n\n## Training (as actually run)\n| | LoRA | QLoRA |\n|---|---|---|\n| rank / alpha / dropout | 16 / 32 / 0.05 | 16 / 32 / 0.05 |\n| target modules | q,k,v,o_proj | q,k,v,o_proj |\n| base precision | bf16 | 4-bit NF4 (double quant), bf16 compute |\n| micro-batch x grad-accum | 4 x 4 | 2 x 8 |\n| learning rate | 2e-4 | 1e-4 |\n| epochs | 3 | 3 |\n\nLoRA and QLoRA differ in learning rate / micro-batch, so their comparison is indicative, not perfectly controlled.\n\n## Evaluation (first {N_EVAL} test questions, greedy decoding, max {MAX_NEW_TOKENS} new tokens, identical settings for every row)\n{df_to_md(table)}\n\n`rouge_l`/`bertscore_f1`: overlap/semantic similarity with short reference answers; `token_f1`: token-level F1;\n`ref_contained`: reference answer appears inside the prediction. Automatic metrics are proxies, not agronomic validation.\n\n## Usage\n```python\nfrom agri_llm import AgriLLM\nllm = AgriLLM(adapters={{\"qlora\": \"<this-repo-or-folder>\"}})\nprint(llm.generate(\"How do I control aphids on cotton?\", mode=\"qlora\"))\n```\n\n## Limitations\nTrained on community-curated Q&A, not agronomist-verified. No retrieval, so it can state wrong facts confidently\n(see failure_candidates.csv). **Research prototype - not a substitute for professional agricultural advice.**\n'''\nopen(f\"{OUT}/MODEL_CARD.md\", \"w\").write(CARD)\nfor name in ADAPTERS:\n    open(f\"{OUT}/adapters/{name}/README.md\", \"w\").write(CARD.replace(\"# Agricultural Q&A adapters\", f\"# Agricultural Q&A adapter [{name}]\", 1))\n\nzip_path = shutil.make_archive(\"/kaggle/working/agri_deploy_bundle\", \"zip\", OUT)\nprint(\"bundle ready:\", zip_path, f\"({os.path.getsize(zip_path) / 1e6:.0f} MB)\")\nprint(sorted(os.listdir(OUT)))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T20:19:47.450251Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T20:19:47.450536Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T20:19:50.566501Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-12T20:19:47.450514Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T20:19:50.565815Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"bundle ready: /kaggle/working/agri_deploy_bundle.zip (40 MB)\n['MODEL_CARD.md', '__pycache__', 'adapters', 'agri_llm.py', 'app_gradio.py', 'eval_predictions.csv', 'eval_scores.json', 'failure_candidates.csv', 'qualitative_comparison.csv', 'requirements.txt']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":31},{"id":"26bfb5ba","cell_type":"code","source":"# OPTIONAL: publish both adapters to the Hugging Face Hub (Kaggle: Add-ons -> Secrets -> HF_TOKEN)\nPUSH_TO_HUB = True\nHF_USERNAME = \"MallikarjunJadi\"\nif PUSH_TO_HUB:\n    from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n    token = UserSecretsClient().get_secret(\"HF_TOKEN\")\n    for name in ADAPTERS:\n        print(push_folder_to_hub(f\"{OUT}/adapters/{name}\", f\"{HF_USERNAME}/qwen2.5-1.5b-agri-q